  <Properties>
    <blocks>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "30a0d072-7837-449e-9db2-228afed80595",
      "key": "87554966-0001-4a01-9c01-000000000001",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "preheading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "About the programme"
        },
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Army JROTC Program Overview"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "<p>The U.S. Army Junior Reserve Officers' Training Corps is one of the world's largest character development and citizenship programmes for youth. The National Defense Act of 1916 first established organised JROTC programmes in schools. Title 10 of the United States Code now requires each military service to run a JROTC programme.</p><p>The programme instils the values of citizenship, service to the United States, and personal responsibility. Its mission, \"to motivate young people to be better citizens\", guides its work in more than 1,700 high schools in the United States and overseas.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "photo",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "links",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "efc614c3-34dd-4262-b6f2-3514575b3ac6",
      "key": "87554966-0007-4a01-9c01-000000000007",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "preheading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "How the programme works"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "accordionList",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ef33a691-ec90-4004-8937-73a37ac2a60c",
                "key": "87554966-0003-4a01-9c01-000000000003",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "alias": "title",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": "The JROTC curriculum"
                  },
                  {
                    "alias": "description",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": {
                      "blocks": {
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": [],
                        "Layout": {}
                      },
                      "markup": "<p>Since 2005 the programme has been accredited as a Special Purpose Program by Cognia (<a href=\"http://www.cognia.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cognia.org</a>). Every lesson uses a four-part model: motivate the cadet, teach new information, practise the skill, then apply it to a real situation. Lessons cover leadership, health and wellness, physical fitness, first aid, geography, American history and government, communication, and emotional intelligence.</p><p>The curriculum meets the Common Core State Standards, and many schools grant core credit for JROTC coursework.</p>"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ef33a691-ec90-4004-8937-73a37ac2a60c",
                "key": "87554966-0004-4a01-9c01-000000000004",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "alias": "title",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": "Co-curricular activities"
                  },
                  {
                    "alias": "description",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": {
                      "blocks": {
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": [],
                        "Layout": {}
                      },
                      "markup": "<p>Cadets take part in activities that reinforce classroom learning:</p><ul><li>Precision and exhibition drill competitions</li><li>Air rifle competitions (optional)</li><li>Raider Challenge competitions</li><li>JROTC Leadership and Academic Bowl</li><li>STEM Camp</li><li>JROTC Cadet Leadership Challenge</li></ul>"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ef33a691-ec90-4004-8937-73a37ac2a60c",
                "key": "87554966-0005-4a01-9c01-000000000005",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "alias": "title",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": "College opportunities"
                  },
                  {
                    "alias": "description",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": {
                      "blocks": {
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": [],
                        "Layout": {}
                      },
                      "markup": "<p>The College Options Foundation helps cadets find colleges that offer credit for completing JROTC. Army ROTC, which is separate from JROTC, offers college scholarships to cadets who qualify. See <a href=\"http://www.collegeoptionsfoundation.net\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">collegeoptionsfoundation.net</a> or <a href=\"https://www.goarmy.com/rotc/high-school-students.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">goarmy.com/rotc</a>.</p>"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ef33a691-ec90-4004-8937-73a37ac2a60c",
                "key": "87554966-0006-4a01-9c01-000000000006",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "alias": "title",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": "National impact"
                  },
                  {
                    "alias": "description",
                    "culture": null,
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": {
                      "blocks": {
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": [],
                        "Layout": {}
                      },
                      "markup": "<p>JROTC tracks five quality indicators. Cadets exceed school averages in every category.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>School</th><th>JROTC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Attendance</td><td>90.29%</td><td>93.54%</td></tr><tr><td>Graduation</td><td>83%</td><td>93.98%</td></tr><tr><td>Indiscipline</td><td>5.2%</td><td>1.7%</td></tr><tr><td>Dropout</td><td>8%</td><td>&lt;1%</td></tr><tr><td>GPA</td><td>2.72</td><td>2.91</td></tr></tbody></table><p>As an accredited Special Purpose Program, JROTC follows Cognia's Standards of Quality and runs the JROTC Program Accreditation review, which documents continuous improvement.</p>"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "87554966-0003-4a01-9c01-000000000003",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
